                "doc": "disputes.md",
                "score": 0.9045,
                "text": "Payment dispute rules\n## Reason codes and chargeback windows\nEach reason code has a window in days from the transaction date. A dispute opened after the window closes is not eligible.\n\n| Reason code | Window (days) |\n|---|---|\n| fraud_card_not_present | 120 |\n| goods_not_received | 90 |\n| duplicate_charge | 60 |\n| service_not_rendered | 90 |\n| unauthorized_debit | 56 |"
              },
              {
                "id": "disputes.md#s3",
                "doc": "disputes.md",
                "score": 0.7845,
                "text": "Payment dispute rules\n## Escalation on blocked disputes\nWhen a dispute is blocked by a customer-level restriction, the case must be\nescalated to a human agent."
              },
              {
                "id": "disputes.md#s2",
                "doc": "disputes.md",
                "score": 0.762,
                "text": "Payment dispute rules\n## Eligibility conditions\nA dispute is eligible only if all of the following hold: the reason code is\nvalid; the transaction status is settled; the transaction date is within the\nreason code's window relative to the current date; and no customer-level\nrestriction applies (for example, an account under compliance review cannot\nopen new disputes until the review concludes)."
              },
              {
                "id": "disputes-process.md#s1",
                "doc": "disputes-process.md",
                "score": 0.7143,
                "text": "Dispute handling process\n## Raising a dispute\nA dispute is raised against a single settled transaction. The customer supplies\nthe transaction reference and a reason code. The agent verifies eligibility\nbefore the case is opened; an ineligible request is refused with the failing\ncondition named, except where confidentiality rules apply."
              }
            ]
          }
        }
